@Vaer

It’s a perfectly coherent suggestion, addressed to Sean (who has been quite active in this comments section recently, and thus is not so unlikely to actually read the suggestion), in the hopes that he might pass it along to the technical wing of the NYT Games meat grinder.

And if you’re genuinely asking for an explanation: the feature request here is for the Games app to select a light vs dark color scheme (ie “light mode” vs “dark mode”) based on what is currently selected in that regard at the operating system level. So, for example, if you open up the Games app on an iPhone at a time when your phone happens to be displaying in “dark mode” (either because you manually selected that, or due to a configured schedule), the Games app will render in “dark mode” as well — and vice versa with “light mode”.
